"3121546","SNV","1","G","T","","Homozygous","16","16","100","0","34","mobile_element: IS6110-11,_len:_1375 nt. Insertion sequence IS6110. This region is a possible MT-complex-specific genomic island (See Becq et al.,_2007)., Misc. feature: similar to insertion sequence element IS6110 transposase(fragment); Putative Transposase for IS6110 (fragment). Identical to many other M. tuberculosis IS6110 transposase subunits. The transposase described here may be made by a frame shifting mechanism during translation, the sequence UUUUAAAG maybe responsible for such a frameshifting event (see McAdam et al.,_1990). This region is a possible MT-complex-specific genomic island (See Becq et al.,_2007 PMID:17545187)., Repeat region: 4392 bp direct repeat region. This region is a possible MT-complex-specific genomic island (See Becq et al.,_2007).","",""
